# =========================================================
# AI-POWERED GENOMICS DASHBOARD
# =========================================================
#
# PROJECT OVERVIEW
# ---------------------------------------------------------
# This application allows users to:
#
# 1. Search for a human gene
# 2. Retrieve genomic data from Ensembl
# 3. Retrieve clinical variant data from ClinVar
# 4. Explore pathogenic/benign variants
# 5. View clinical evidence summaries
#
# This project combines:
# - Bioinformatics
# - API integration
# - Data visualization
# - Full-stack application structure
# - Clinical genomics concepts
#
# =========================================================
# STREAMLIT ARCHITECTURE NOTES
# =========================================================
#
# IMPORTANT:
# Streamlit reruns the ENTIRE script whenever:
# - a button is clicked
# - a dropdown changes
# - text input changes
#
# Because of this, we use:
#
# st.session_state
#
# to preserve data between reruns.
#
# Example:
#
# st.session_state.page
#
# stores which "page" the user is currently on.
#
# =========================================================
# SESSION STATE VARIABLES
# =========================================================
#
# page
# ----
# Tracks which page the user is viewing.
#
# Example:
# "home"
# "variants"
#
#
# gene_symbol
# -----------
# Stores the currently searched gene.
#
#
# variants_df
# -----------
# Stores the ClinVar dataframe returned from the API.
#
#
# selected_variant
# ----------------
# Stores the currently selected variant so it can
# be accessed across pages.
#
# =========================================================
# ENSEMBL API NOTES
# =========================================================
#
# Ensembl provides genomic annotation data.
#
# Endpoint used:
#
# /lookup/symbol/homo_sapiens/{gene}
#
# Example:
# BRCA1
# TP53
#
# Returns:
# - chromosome
# - start/end positions
# - Ensembl gene ID
# - gene biotype
#
# Documentation:
# https://rest.ensembl.org
#
# =========================================================
# CLINVAR API NOTES
# =========================================================
#
# ClinVar contains:
# - disease-associated variants
# - pathogenicity classifications
# - clinical review evidence
#
# We use NCBI E-utilities:
#
# 1. esearch
#    -> search for ClinVar IDs
#
# 2. esummary
#    -> retrieve metadata for those IDs
#
# Example classifications:
# - Pathogenic
# - Likely pathogenic
# - Benign
# - Uncertain significance
#
# Documentation:
# https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/clinvar/
#
# =========================================================
# BIOINFORMATICS NOTES
# =========================================================
#
# GENE
# ----
# A region of DNA encoding biological function.
#
#
# VARIANT
# -------
# A change in DNA sequence.
#
#
# CLINICAL SIGNIFICANCE
# ---------------------
# Measures how strongly a variant is associated
# with disease.
#
#
# REVIEW STATUS
# -------------
# Indicates confidence/evidence level for
# a clinical interpretation.
#
#
# PATHOGENIC
# ----------
# Variant likely contributes to disease.
#
#
# BENIGN
# ------
# Variant unlikely to contribute to disease.
#
#
# VUS
# ---
# Variant of Uncertain Significance.
#
# =========================================================
# DATAFLOW OF THE APP
# =========================================================
#
# User enters gene
#        ↓
# Ensembl API called
#        ↓
# ClinVar API called
#        ↓
# Variants loaded into dataframe
#        ↓
# User selects variant
#        ↓
# Clinical evidence displayed
#
